Based on my exploration, dnsscienced already has extensive security features built in. Here are additional security capabilities we can add:

  High-Priority Security Enhancements

  1. DNSSEC Validation (Critical Gap)

  - Full DNSSEC signature verification
  - Algorithm downgrade protection
  - Trust anchor management
  - NSEC3 iteration limits
  - Key rollover handling

  Impact: Ensures DNS responses haven't been tampered with in transit

  2. Extended DNS Errors (RFC 8914)

  - Detailed error codes for security events
  - Better debugging and forensics
  - Client-side security awareness

  Impact: Improves troubleshooting and security visibility

  3. Query Name Minimization (RFC 7816)

  - The function exists in internal/engine/security.go:114 but isn't integrated
  - Would reduce query exposure to intermediate nameservers

  Impact: Enhanced privacy protection

  4. TSIG Authentication (RFC 8945)

  - Cryptographic authentication for zone transfers
  - Secure dynamic updates
  - Peer-to-peer authentication

  Impact: Prevents unauthorized zone modifications

  Advanced Security Features

  5. DNS Firewall Enhancements

  - Behavioral anomaly detection: ML-based detection of unusual query patterns
  - Geofencing: Block/allow queries based on GeoIP
  - Regex-based RPZ rules: More flexible filtering patterns
  - Real-time threat feed integration: Multiple TI providers with scoring aggregation

  6. Zero-Trust Architecture

  - Per-client authentication: mTLS for DoT/DoH clients
  - JWT-based query authorization: API-style access control
  - Audit logging: Comprehensive query logs with security context

  7. Network Protocol Security

  - DNS over QUIC (DoQ) - RFC 9250 (more efficient than DoT)
  - Oblivious DoH (ODoH) - RFC 9230 (zero-knowledge privacy)
  - TLS 1.3 with 0-RTT for DoT/DoH (performance + security)

  8. Advanced DDoS Protection

  - SYN flood protection: TCP connection rate limiting
  - Query complexity scoring: Penalize expensive queries (wildcards, ANY)
  - Proof-of-work challenges: For clients during attack
  - IP reputation scoring: Dynamic rate limits based on past behavior

  9. Data Loss Prevention & Exfiltration Detection

  - DNS tunneling detection: Statistical analysis of payload sizes
  - Subdomain enumeration detection: Track excessive NXDOMAIN patterns
  - Data exfiltration alerts: Detect base64/hex-encoded subdomains

  10. Compliance & Forensics

  - Query auditing: GDPR-compliant logging with PII redaction
  - Forensic query replay: Reconstruct attack timelines
  - Compliance reporting: SOC2/ISO27001 audit trails
  - SIEM integration: Syslog/JSON output to security platforms

